WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.524
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level three.

2
00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:09.547
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:16.970
Unit sixteen: Political Ideologies. Today you will recognise belief, person and adjective forms with suffixes.

4
00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.922
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:24.227
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:26.247
Conservatism.

7
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.724
Conservatism means a belief in tradition and gradual change.

8
00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:35.592
Conservatism values stability and established institutions.

9
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:38.812
Your turn. Say: Conservatism.

10
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:42.970
Conservatism.

11
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:44.857
Liberalism.

12
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.556
Liberalism means a belief in individual freedom and equal rights.

13
00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.463
Liberalism protects freedom of speech.

14
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.668
Your turn. Say: Liberalism.

15
00:00:58.533 --> 00:00:59.500
Liberalism.

16
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.507
Socialism.

17
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:06.699
Socialism means a belief in shared ownership and greater equality.

18
00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:10.258
Socialism supports strong public services.

19
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.293
Your turn. Say: Socialism.

20
00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:17.169
Socialism.

21
00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:19.289
Political spectrum.

22
00:01:20.283 --> 00:01:24.199
Political spectrum means the range of political beliefs from left to right.

23
00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:27.677
The party sits near the centre of the political spectrum.

24
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:31.539
Your turn. Say: Political spectrum.

25
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.912
Political spectrum.

26
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:37.802
Ideology.

27
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:42.476
Ideology means a set of beliefs about how society should work.

28
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:45.907
An ideology can guide a party's decisions.

29
00:01:46.517 --> 00:01:49.041
Your turn. Say: Ideology.

30
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.982
Ideology.

31
00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:55.031
Political values.

32
00:01:56.017 --> 00:02:00.280
Political values means the principles that shape a person's political opinions.

33
00:02:00.883 --> 00:02:03.359
Her political values emphasise fairness.

34
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.020
Your turn. Say: Political values.

35
00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:11.158
Political values.

36
00:02:11.917 --> 00:02:13.162
Party platform.

37
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.100
Party platform means a party's official list of goals and policies.

38
00:02:18.717 --> 00:02:21.169
The party platform promised lower taxes.

39
00:02:21.783 --> 00:02:24.540
Your turn. Say: Party platform.

40
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.668
Party platform.

41
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:30.847
Policy position.

42
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:35.905
Policy position means a stated view on a specific political issue.

43
00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:39.631
His policy position on housing surprised supporters.

44
00:02:40.217 --> 00:02:42.973
Your turn. Say: Policy position.

45
00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:47.218
Policy position.

46
00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:51.568
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:57.844
Visal, we say 'conservatism', 'conservative' and 'a conservative'. How can I tell the forms apart?

48
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:17.792
Suffixes show the word class. -ism makes an abstract noun for a belief: liberalism, socialism. -ist or -ian names the person: a socialist, a politician. -ive and -al make adjectives: conservative, liberal.

49
00:03:18.883 --> 00:03:20.384
Do spellings change?

50
00:03:21.483 --> 00:03:37.852
Often. Stress shifts too: LIB-er-al, LIB-er-al-ism, but con-SERV-a-tive. And 'ideology' becomes 'ideological', not 'ideologic'. Check each word in a dictionary.

51
00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.031
Why does this matter in politics?

52
00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:55.148
A careful writer separates the belief, the person and the description: a socialist party defends socialism with socialist policies. Mixing them confuses readers.

53
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.137
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:58.983 --> 00:04:03.932
Grammar focus: Word formation: -ism and -ist and -ive and -al.

55
00:04:04.232 --> 00:04:05.546
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:11.117
Liberal + -ism = liberalism, a belief in individual freedom.

57
00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:15.909
A socialist party defends socialism through socialist policies.

58
00:04:16.817 --> 00:04:20.534
The party's platform is conservative on tax and liberal on rights.

59
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:31.710
-ism = belief (noun), -ist / -ian = follower (noun), -al / -ive / -ic = adjective. Learn the whole family: conserve, conservatism, conservative, conservationist.

60
00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:36.275
Be careful! Don't say: He is a strong liberalism.

61
00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:40.570
Say: He is a strong liberal.

62
00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:43.949
-ism names the belief; use -al for the person.

63
00:04:44.733 --> 00:04:47.734
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:50.846
Left, Right and Everything Between.

65
00:04:51.146 --> 00:04:55.340
An ideology is a set of ideas about how society should be organised.

66
00:04:56.333 --> 00:05:04.451
Conservatism values tradition, liberalism stresses individual freedom, and socialism emphasises shared ownership and equality.

67
00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:12.052
The political spectrum places these beliefs from left to right, but real citizens rarely sit at a single point.

68
00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:20.395
A party platform may be conservative on taxes and liberal on rights, so each policy position needs separate study.

69
00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.990
Political values, not labels, should guide an informed voter.

70
00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:30.102
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.704
Someone who follows socialism is a blank.

72
00:05:34.004 --> 00:05:37.890
A, socialist. B, socialism. C, socially.

73
00:05:41.433 --> 00:05:43.897
The answer is A: socialist.

74
00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:48.071
The abstract noun for a belief in freedom is blank.

75
00:05:48.371 --> 00:05:52.059
A, liberal. B, liberalism. C, liberate.

76
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.122
The answer is B: liberalism.

77
00:05:59.283 --> 00:06:02.305
The adjective form of 'conserve' in politics is blank.

78
00:06:02.605 --> 00:06:06.885
A, conservatism. B, conservationist. C, conservative.

79
00:06:10.433 --> 00:06:12.909
The answer is C: conservative.

80
00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.829
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:16.129 --> 00:06:22.395
A, He is a strong liberalism.. B, He is a strong liberal.. C, He is a strong liberally..

82
00:06:25.933 --> 00:06:28.757
The answer is B: He is a strong liberal..

83
00:06:29.917 --> 00:06:33.797
According to the reading, an informed voter should follow political…

84
00:06:34.097 --> 00:06:37.994
A, values. B, labels. C, slogans.

85
00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:43.672
The answer is A: values.

86
00:06:44.867 --> 00:06:47.879
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:48.717 --> 00:06:52.829
Do you think most people fit neatly into a single political ideology?

88
00:07:01.617 --> 00:07:03.082
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:31.106
I do not think most people fit neatly into one ideology. People often hold mixed views, such as supporting free markets but also strong public healthcare. Their opinions are shaped by family, experience, religion and local problems, not only by party labels. The political spectrum is a helpful simplification, but real values are usually more complex and can change over time.

90
00:07:31.406 --> 00:07:33.092
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:33.983 --> 00:07:40.107
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and word formation: -ism and -ist and -ive and -al.

92
00:07:40.407 --> 00:07:45.219
Today's value is respectful disagreement. Disagree politely and listen to others.

93
00:07:45.519 --> 00:07:48.229
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:48.529 --> 00:07:51.332
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

